<!--
  ComboboxFloatingDemo.rozie — content-STABLE flipped-popup screenshot fixture for
  the pure-Rozie Combobox (Phase 86 R2, plan 86-03).

  The one thing a happy-dom mount-and-drive behavioral test (floating-popover.
  behavior.test.ts) cannot prove: an actual VIEWPORT-EDGE flip, since happy-dom has
  no layout engine. This demo exists ONLY to make that flip a deterministic pixel
  cell — never extend it for behavior (mirrors ComboboxScreenshotDemo.rozie's own
  "never bolt behavior onto the screenshot cell" discipline, inverted).

  Made deterministic by:
    1. A tall (680px), explicitly-sized root box with the control pushed near its
       BOTTOM via `padding-top`. The Playwright viewport pinned for this suite is
       1280×720 (playwright.config.ts) and `rozie-mount` starts at the very top of
       the page (no chrome above it), so an input sitting ~600-640px down leaves
       only ~80-120px of viewport space below it — less than the four-option
       popup's rendered height, so Floating UI's `flip` middleware (the composed
       @rozie-ui/popover leaf's default) relocates the popup ABOVE the input.
    2. The root box's OWN explicit height (not auto-sized from flow content) is
       what keeps the flipped-up popup inside `[data-testid="rozie-mount"]`'s
       captured bounding box: `position: absolute` content does not grow an
       ancestor's auto height, so if the root box were only as tall as the input
       itself, the popup — rendered visually ABOVE that box's top edge — would fall
       OUTSIDE Playwright's element-screenshot crop region and never be captured.
    3. A FIXED four-option list (apple/banana/cherry/date — the same set
       ComboboxScreenshotDemo.rozie uses) with NO pre-selected value, so the
       popup's content is identical across all six targets and every re-run.
    4. The popup is opened DETERMINISTICALLY at mount via the composed Combobox's
       own `focus` handle — `$refs.floatingCombobox.focus()`, deferred one
       macrotask (setTimeout(0)) past `$onMount` for the SAME reason
       ToasterScreenshotDemo.rozie defers its `$refs.toaster.show()` call: a
       child's $expose handle is not yet registered when a PARENT's $onMount
       runs synchronously on Solid (children-before-parent mount + ref-readiness
       timing) — a synchronous call there no-ops and the popup never opens. A
       screenshot cell cannot click/focus from the spec side the way a
       behavioral cell would, so it must self-open on mount.

  One .rozie source compiles to six per-framework screenshot consumers; the Linux
  PNG baseline is generated separately in pinned Linux Docker (NOT here —
  feedback_vr_linux_baselines). Until it lands the matrix cell auto-fixmes on
  `baselineExists()`.
-->

<rozie name="ComboboxFloatingDemo">

<components>
{
  Combobox: '../../packages/ui/combobox/src/Combobox.rozie',
}
</components>

<data>
{
  value: null,
}
</data>

<script>
const OPTIONS = [
  { value: 'apple', label: 'Apple' },
  { value: 'banana', label: 'Banana' },
  { value: 'cherry', label: 'Cherry' },
  { value: 'date', label: 'Date' },
]

// See the header comment (point 4) for why this is deferred one macrotask past
// $onMount rather than called synchronously.
$onMount(() => {
  setTimeout(() => {
    $refs.floatingCombobox.focus()
  }, 0)
})
</script>

<template>
<div class="combobox-floating-demo">
  <Combobox
    ref="floatingCombobox"
    r-model:value="$data.value"
    :options="OPTIONS"
    placeholder="Search fruit…"
    ariaLabel="Fruit"
    idBase="floating-combobox"
  />
</div>
</template>

<style>
.combobox-floating-demo {
  box-sizing: border-box;
  font-family: system-ui, -apple-system, sans-serif;
  color: #1a1a1a;
  width: 360px;
  height: 680px;
  padding: 1rem;
  padding-top: 600px;
}
</style>

</rozie>
